# SCHLAR — PROMPT 4: COMPLETE VICE PRINCIPAL & TEACHER WORKSPACES

## PROJECT CONTEXT

Continue developing the existing SCHLAR School Management System in this same Google AI Studio project.

Prompts 1–3 have been completed. Prompt 1 established the brand and theme system. Prompt 2 established the application architecture, role selection, navigation, and permission system. Prompt 3 established the Admin workspace and core school operations.

Your task is to implement **Prompt 4: the complete Vice Principal and Teacher workspaces**.

This is a continuation of an existing application, not a new project. First inspect the current codebase, routes, components, data models, theme system, permissions, and completed Admin functionality. Reuse the existing architecture and extend it carefully.

## 1. NON-NEGOTIABLE REQUIREMENTS

1. Preserve all working functionality from Prompts 1–3.
2. Do not redesign or replace the existing Admin workspace.
3. Do not introduce new roles.
4. Keep Vice Principal and Teacher as separate roles with different permissions.
5. Use the existing SCHLAR design system and theme engine, including all 12 palettes and custom theme settings.
6. Use existing navigation and routing patterns where possible.
7. Implement real interactive frontend workflows, not static screenshots or decorative mockups.
8. Do not make every sidebar item a folder. Keep important destinations direct and group related subpages into expandable folders where appropriate.
9. Do not place every feature into one oversized page. Use dedicated list, detail, creation, editing, and report pages.
10. Use shared school data consistently. A change made through one authorized workflow should be reflected in other relevant views.
11. Do not claim real authentication, server synchronization, notifications, or backend security if these are not implemented.
12. Do not report tests as passed unless they were actually run.

Core design principle:

**Make every screen simple enough for a first-time user, but make the system powerful enough for a real school. Simplify navigation and workflows, not functionality or permissions.**

